# Re-include this project's appsettings files. The parent .gitignore ignores all `appsettings.*`
# (to keep secret-bearing config out of git), but here secrets live in .env (gitignored) and
# user-secrets — the appsettings files are secret-free, so they should be tracked and shared.
# A .gitignore in a deeper directory overrides the parent, and negating file patterns re-includes them.
!appsettings.json
!appsettings.*.json
